## Android adaptation coverage

- Android-style status/navigation insets and phone presentation
- Android Back: close overlay first, route history second, exit confirmation at Breeder Home
- contextual Breeder Quick Log as bottom sheet
- Breeder Round execution and summary
- Photo Picker-first media entry
- camera permission requested only for new capture
- contextual notification permission
- notification deep links to exact breeder context
- offline breeder write queue and single-result reconciliation
- local draft restoration after process restart
- fail-closed stale/unavailable breeder context
- shared Journal event identity presentation
- 360 / 390 / 430 mobile viewport behavior

## Breeder Round authority boundary

The Android prototype does **not** redesign the Breeder Round queue model. It inherits holistic Breeder v0.2:

`ROUND_QUEUE = DUE_AND_OVERDUE_SCHEDULED_WORK + ROUTINE_ACTIVE_BREEDING_CONTEXTS`

Context determines the available rapid actions. Consequential records such as counts, moves, splits and hatch records use structured forms.

